  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-p2100.html",
  "prefLabel": "He-P 2102.06 Source Water",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-P 2102.06 Source Water. To assure that the source used by a plant for bottled water is in compliance with the quality standards set forth in He-P 2102.02, the plant or bulk source ownership shall collect or direct the collection of samples of source water for analysis, in accordance with 21 CFR 129.35, as follows:\n\n(a) For chemical and physical standards, samples of source water shall be collected and analyzed at least once each calendar year;\n\n(b) For radiological standards, samples of source water shall be collected and analyzed at least once every 4 years; and\n\n(c) For microbiological standards, samples of source water shall be collected and analyzed at least once each calendar year if the source is a public water supply, or once each week if the source is not a public water supply.\n\nSource. #12680, eff 11-27-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-p2100.html"
}
